  "conclusion": "DirectShow/FFmpeg mode changes from 320x240 to 1280x720 did not change its approximately 7.4 FPS wall rate. OpenCV Media Foundation capture is substantially faster, but the latest 352x288 pixel-read first-frame-to-loop-end measurement is 27.868 active FPS with 138.782 ms read-completion p95, below the 30 FPS gate and with bursty delivery. A 60-second grab-only measurement reached 29.9327 grabs per active second, still below 30 FPS and with 141.377 ms p95; it does not retrieve image pixels or test encoding/stego. These sequential host diagnostics do not establish camera sensor timing, zero drops, strict H.264 validity, HTTP latency, or edge-device acceptance."
